.page uname 1 print system information

# SYNOPSIS
*uname* [*-asnrvmpc*]

# DESCRIPTION
`uname` prints facts about the running system. With no option it prints the kernel name.

# OPTIONS
@ *-s*
    The kernel name (`Gensokyo`).
@ *-n*
    The node name: the host name.
@ *-r*
    The kernel release.
@ *-v*
    The kernel version string.
@ *-m*, *-p*
    The machine hardware name.
@ *-c*
    The release's code name, named after a game of the series (an extension of this system).
@ *-a*, *--all*
    Everything above, in that order.

# EXAMPLES
    uname -a
    uname -sr

# SEE ALSO
hostname(1), uptime(1), gensokyo(7)
